-1 STARTING~
If you're interested in getting started on PKMud, keep reading, since it
will save you from bugging other players somewhat.  Here are what I feel
are the most asked and important questions:
1) Why can't I lift an arm? (do anything?)
    - You are not in the war.  To participate, log on before one starts
      and you are automatically placed in.  You may also join within 10
      minutes of the war's start, but you will not be restored.  Kindly
      request a restore over chat and a god will most likely heal you if
      one is on.
2) What are the classes and races here?
    - There are no races on PKMud.  To see a list of classes, type 'help
      changeclass', and choose one which suits you.  I would recommend 
      trying them all out at least once.
3) What do i do after i kill someone?
    - First of all, you most likely will want to examine the corpse, and 
      whatever seems useful (gold, eq, etc).  Then, most importantly, you
      should always sacrifice the corpse to Rip, and he rewards you with
      a quart of fresh blood (400 hp/mana restore).
4) Why is my char deleted every time i come back?
    - This is because in order to save on PKMud, you have to at least kill
      2 people.
5) Is there a map? Yes.  type help map.
~


-1 EXPLORE NEWPLAYER~
One of the most imporant parts to player killing is the hunt.  Because
of this, we have made several modifications to allow players to map
the MUD easier.  The 'GOTO' command is now usable by mortals. You use
it by typing 'goto <mob>', where mob is the name of the monster you want to
find.  The 'TELEPORT' command is useful for exploring random locations.
The 'RECALL' command teleports you to the temple of Ys.

Other commands players should be aware of are WHERE, CHANGECLASS, and
USERS.  (WHERE and CHANGECLASS have help files, USERS is simply a nice
version of WHO that tells you what site people are from, for catching
people playing multiples.)

Also, if you have never played a Diku, you should likely read the help files
for CAST, BASH, etc..  When you use the CHANGECLASS command, you can
assess the classes strengths and weaknesses by using SCORE and PRACTICE.
SCORE will show you that classes max hit points and mana, PRACTICE will
give you a list of skills that class knows.

If you have any questions, ask someone who is on!!
~

-1 NEWS~
There are no aliases here, please do: help tintin

Food/Drink and Movement were removed, if you see anything remaining of
these, please post somewhere.

Thirst was removed, but drinking has some neat affects... try it out.
(The cost of most drinks ought to give you a hint as to what they do ;)

Special procedures added to objects.  The One ring and winged boots
are two examples...  Note that spec proc objects do _not_ give you
any message when the proc kicks in...  so pay careful attention to
score.

Please see help news2.
~

-1 NEWS2~

Mob damage/hit points were changed to a more standard Diku amount.
Note that I am about to implement non-simple mobs (ie: ones that
don't use the S flag in the .zon files) so some mobs may or may not
continue to act normal...

Some potions, scrolls and wands may give you special abilities.

The War system now works, read help Start.

Most decent equipment is way limited now...  I would suggest killing
with what you start with...

Please see news3.
~

-1 NEWS3~

Where works different now, but costs money, see help where.

Shops now have unlimited money.
Hint:  The maid in south midgaard sells drinks.

Noplay added, see help noplay.

Assassins now do more damage on backstabs.

Please see NEWS4.
~

0 NEWS4~
Wars are now one hour.  Ticks are still 30 seconds.

Sanct was removed from a bunch of mobs, if you spot a sancted mob,
post it somewhere.

Any lock can now be picked.

You can now sell stuff while invis.

'Someones' no longer arrive and leave.  If you spot anything else someones
should not do... note it somewhere.

Please see NEWS5.
~


0 NEWS5~
Dead people can kinda see invis now.  If you know of something you
can't see, post it somewhere.

Finger command added, victim has to be connected tho...

Changeclass command added.

Please leave a note or email peckham@hurricane.seas.ucla.edu if
you see anything that needs fixing.
~



-1 STORY~
One day, I got bored and decided mobs really really sucked, this
war years ago...  One day not long ago February 1994, I got even
more bored and decided to give non-wimp players a challenge, so
I started hacking away on this bit of code...   (oh, non-wimp means
that if you prefer team wars on genocide rather than A wars, you
are a wimp.  If you need a reg to do your killing for you... you
are not a PK... dig?)

So I need to come up with a story, ok, one day, there was this like,
nuclear explosion, set of by, heh heheh, Beavis, and he like, burned
all the mobs, and they got all frail and weak.  So the players got
bored and like, started burning each other, at least the mages and
clerics did, the thieves started stabbing everyone in the back, and
the warriors started hacking away with swords...  This all degenerated
into a mosh, and some like, ultra powerful valley speaking aliens
landed and said, 'Hey dude!.'  Then this guy from the band Scatterbrain
came up and said 'Hey dude, don't call me dude!' and smacked the alien
upside one of this four heads.  That was the end of all the aliens, no,
I won't elaborate, it just makes sense that if you knock 25% of the blocks
off of one alien, that all of them will submit to your rule.  So the
aliens were pissed, and sent for backup.  However, the Predator came
down and wanted one champion in less than an hour who would represent
the Earth versus him.  So, he gave the ultimatum that if the Earth didn't
have a champion in an hour, he would blow it up.  Lot's of people wanted
to be champion (those would be you..) and all fought it out with each
other...  The funny thing was, everytime either the world got blown
up, or a champion was picked, everyone lost link and had to reconnect
a few minutes later to decide again...

Well that was a stupid story...

Rip

~



